# Inventory Management System

A modern, full-stack inventory management solution designed for warehouses and businesses to efficiently track, manage, and locate inventory stock. Built with Next.js for a responsive frontend experience and Express.js for a robust backend API.

## 🚀 Features

- **Real-time Inventory Tracking** - Monitor stock levels and locations in real-time
- **Advanced Search & Filtering** - Quickly locate items across multiple warehouses
- **Multi-workspace Support** - Manage inventory across different workspaces
- **User Authentication & Authorization** - Secure role-based access control
- **RESTful API** - Comprehensive backend API for inventory operations
- **Responsive Design** - Access from desktop, tablet, or mobile devices
- **Database Management** - Powered by Prisma ORM with MySQL
- **Redis Caching** - Fast session management and data caching
- **File Storage** - MinIO S3-compatible object storage
- **Subscription Management** - Built-in subscription and workspace management

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

### Frontend

- **Next.js 15** - React framework with server-side rendering
- **TypeScript** - Type-safe development
- **Tailwind CSS** - Modern utility-first styling
- **Shadcn/ui** - Beautiful, accessible UI components

### Backend

- **Express.js** - Fast, minimalist web framework
- **TypeScript** - Full type safety across the stack
- **Prisma ORM** - Type-safe database client
- **MySQL 8.0** - Relational database
- **Redis** - Session store and caching
- **Passport.js** - Authentication middleware

### DevOps & Infrastructure

- **Docker & Docker Compose** - Containerized development and production environments
- **Traefik** - Reverse proxy and load balancer
- **MinIO** - S3-compatible object storage with replication support
- **Automated Backups** - Scheduled MySQL dumps to MinIO

## 📋 Prerequisites

Before you begin, ensure you have the following installed:

- **Node.js** (v22 or higher)
- **pnpm** (v8 or higher) - `npm install -g pnpm`
- **Docker** & **Docker Compose**
- **Git**

## 🔧 Installation

### 1. Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/SpaceWaffles5827/inventory-app.git
cd inventory-app
```

### 2. Install Dependencies
```bash
pnpm install
```

### 3. Environment Configuration

Create a `.dev.env` file in the root directory for development:
```env
########################################
# == Ports / Published/Internal ==
########################################
# Chosen to avoid existing bindings:
# in use: 3001, 3005, 3069, 6382, 8080, 80, 81, 443, 9000, 9001
TRAEFIK_HTTP_PORT=3069
TRAEFIK_DASHBOARD_PORT=8082

APP_INTERNAL_PORT=3000
SERVER_INTERNAL_PORT=5001

MYSQL_PORT=3308
REDIS_PORT=6382

MINIO_API_PORT=9000
MINIO_CONSOLE_PORT=9003


########################################
# == Disaster Recovery (DR MinIO) ==
########################################
DR_ENDPOINT=http://backup-host:9000
DR_MINIO_ROOT_USER=minioadmin
DR_MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=minioadmin
DR_BUCKET_NAME=inventory-app

# 1 = allow plain HTTP for mc (only if DR endpoint is http)
MC_INSECURE=1


########################################
# == MySQL ==
########################################
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=your-secure-root-password
MYSQL_DATABASE=inventory_software_dev
MYSQL_USER=appuser
MYSQL_PASSWORD=your-secure-app-password
MYSQL_ROOT_HOST=%

# When running tools from host, use localhost + published port.
# In containers, service DNS is "mysql" and port 3306.
MYSQL_HOST=localhost

# Prisma URLs (parameterized ports/hosts)
DATABASE_URL=mysql://${MYSQL_USER}:${MYSQL_PASSWORD}@${MYSQL_HOST}:${MYSQL_PORT}/${MYSQL_DATABASE}
DATABASE_URL_ROOT=mysql://root:${MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD}@${MYSQL_HOST}:${MYSQL_PORT}/${MYSQL_DATABASE}
SHADOW_DATABASE_URL=mysql://root:${MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD}@${MYSQL_HOST}:${MYSQL_PORT}/inventory_software_dev_shadow


########################################
# == Redis ==
########################################
# For host tooling use 127.0.0.1 + published port; 
# in containers use host "redis" and port 6379.
REDIS_HOST=127.0.0.1


########################################
# == MinIO (Local) ==
########################################
MINIO_ROOT_USER=minioadmin
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=your-secure-minio-password
BUCKET_NAME=inventory-app
BUCKET_REGION=us-east-1

# Service URL for SDKs that expect S3-style endpoint
MINIO_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:${MINIO_API_PORT}


########################################
# == App Misc ==
########################################
DEV_MODE=true
SESSION_SECRET=your-long-random-secret-min-32-chars
USER_ID_ADMIN_MYSQL=your-admin-user-id
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION=0.0.0

# App URLs
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:${SERVER_INTERNAL_PORT}
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:${APP_INTERNAL_PORT}
BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:${SERVER_INTERNAL_PORT}
APP_URL_IOS=https://apps.apple.com/us/app/inventory-app/id0000000000


########################################
# == Email ==
########################################
DONOTREPLY_EMAIL=support@yourdomain.com
GOOGLE_EMAIL_USER=support@yourdomain.com
GOOGLE_APP_PASSWORD=your-google-app-password
```

**Security Note:** Generate secure secrets:
```bash
# Generate a secure session secret (min 32 characters)
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"

# Generate a secure admin user ID
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(12).toString('base64url'))"
```

### 4. Initialize Database

Create your initial database migration:
```bash
npx prisma migrate dev --name init
```

This will create the database schema and generate migration files.

### 5. Start the Application
```bash
pnpm dev
```

This command will:

1. Start Docker containers (MySQL, Redis, MinIO, Traefik)
2. Wait for the database to be ready
3. Sync Prisma schema with the database
4. Start the Next.js frontend (port 3000)
5. Start the Express backend (port 5001)

## 🚀 Available Scripts

### Development
```bash
# Start the full development environment
pnpm dev

# Start only the Docker stack (databases, Redis, MinIO, Traefik)
pnpm stack:up

# Start only the frontend
pnpm dev:front

# Start only the backend
pnpm dev:back

# Sync Prisma schema with database
pnpm prisma:sync
```

### Production
```bash
# Build Docker images and start production environment
pnpm prod:build

# Start production environment (without rebuilding)
pnpm prod

# Build TypeScript server code
pnpm server:build

# Start compiled server
pnpm server:start

# Build Next.js application
pnpm build

# Start Next.js production server
pnpm start
```

### Code Quality
```bash
# Run ESLint
pnpm lint

# Type check without emitting files
pnpm type-check
```

### Database Management
```bash
# Generate Prisma Client
npx prisma generate

# Create a new migration
npx prisma migrate dev --name migration_name

# Deploy migrations to production
npx prisma migrate deploy

# Reset database (WARNING: destroys all data)
npx prisma migrate reset

# Open Prisma Studio (database GUI)
npx prisma studio
```

## 📂 Project Structure
```
inventory-app/
├── app/                    # Next.js app directory (pages, layouts)
│   ├── dashboard/          # Dashboard pages
│   ├── accept-invitation/  # Invitation acceptance flow
│   └── login/              # Authentication pages
├── server/                 # Express.js backend
│   ├── controllers/        # Route controllers
│   ├── routes/             # API routes
│   ├── utils/              # Utility functions
│   ├── middleware/         # Custom middleware
│   ├── types/              # TypeScript type definitions
│   ├── tsconfig.json       # Server-specific TypeScript config
│   └── index.ts            # Server entry point
├── prisma/                 # Database schema and migrations
│   ├── schema.prisma       # Prisma schema definition
│   └── migrations/         # Database migration files
├── components/             # React components
│   └── ui/                 # Shadcn UI components
├── lib/                    # Shared utilities
│   └── api/                # API client functions
├── docker-compose.dev.yml  # Development Docker configuration
├── docker-compose.yml      # Production Docker configuration
├── docker-compose.build.yml # Build configuration for production
├── Dockerfile.app          # Next.js app Docker build
├── Dockerfile.server       # Express server Docker build
├── .dockerignore           # Docker ignore patterns
├── next.config.ts          # Next.js configuration
├── tsconfig.json           # Root TypeScript configuration
├── .dev.env                # Development environment variables
└── .env                    # Production environment variables
```

## 🔌 API Endpoints

### Authentication

- `POST /api/auth/register` - Register new user
- `POST /api/auth/login` - User login
- `POST /api/auth/logout` - User logout
- `GET /api/auth/me` - Get current user
- `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` - Request password reset
- `POST /api/auth/reset-password` - Reset password

### Workspaces

- `GET /api/workspaces` - List user's workspaces
- `POST /api/workspaces` - Create new workspace
- `GET /api/workspaces/:id` - Get workspace details
- `PUT /api/workspaces/:id` - Update workspace
- `DELETE /api/workspaces/:id` - Delete workspace

### Invitations

- `POST /api/invitations` - Send workspace invitation
- `GET /api/invitations/verify` - Verify invitation token
- `POST /api/invitations/accept` - Accept invitation
- `DELETE /api/invitations/:id` - Cancel invitation

### Inventory

- `GET /api/items` - List inventory items
- `POST /api/items` - Create new item
- `GET /api/items/:id` - Get item details
- `PATCH /api/items/:id` - Update item
- `DELETE /api/items/:id` - Delete item

### Categories

- `GET /api/categories` - List categories
- `POST /api/categories` - Create category
- `PATCH /api/categories/:id` - Update category
- `DELETE /api/categories/:id` - Delete category

### Locations

- `GET /api/locations` - List locations
- `POST /api/locations` - Create location
- `PATCH /api/locations/:id` - Update location
- `DELETE /api/locations/:id` - Delete location

### Suppliers

- `GET /api/suppliers` - List suppliers
- `POST /api/suppliers` - Create supplier
- `GET /api/suppliers/:id` - Get supplier details
- `PATCH /api/suppliers/:id` - Update supplier
- `DELETE /api/suppliers/:id` - Delete supplier

### Transactions

- `GET /api/transactions` - List stock transactions
- `POST /api/transactions` - Create transaction

### Health Check

- `GET /api/alive` - Server health check

## 🗄️ Database

The application uses **MySQL 8.0** with **Prisma ORM** for type-safe database access.

### Data Model

- **Users** - User accounts and authentication
- **Workspaces** - Multi-tenant workspace isolation
- **WorkspaceMembers** - User-workspace relationships with roles
- **Subscriptions** - Workspace subscription management
- **Items** - Inventory items
- **Categories** - Item categorization
- **Locations** - Storage locations
- **Suppliers** - Supplier information
- **StockTransactions** - Inventory movement tracking
- **Invitations** - Workspace invitation system
- **AuthEvents** - Security audit logging

## 🐳 Docker Services

### Development Environment (`docker-compose.dev.yml`)

- **Traefik** (ports 3069, 8082) - Reverse proxy and dashboard
- **MySQL** (port 3308) - Primary database
- **Redis** (port 6382) - Session storage and caching
- **MinIO** (ports 9000, 9003) - S3-compatible object storage

### Production Environment (`docker-compose.yml`)

In addition to the development services, production includes:

- **App Container** - Next.js application
- **Server Container** - Express.js API
- **Prisma Migrate** - Automated database migrations
- **MinIO Setup** - Automated bucket creation
- **MySQL Backup** - Automated nightly backups to MinIO
- **MinIO Replication** - Disaster recovery replication (optional)

Access services:

- **Application**: http://localhost:3069 (via Traefik)
- **Traefik Dashboard**: http://localhost:8082
- **MinIO Console**: http://localhost:9003
- **API**: http://localhost:3069/api (via Traefik)

## 🔐 Authentication & Security

- **Passport.js** - Local authentication strategy
- **bcrypt** - Secure password hashing
- **express-session** - Session management with Redis
- **2FA Support** - Two-factor authentication via email
- **Password Reset** - Secure password reset flow
- **Helmet** - Security headers
- **CORS** - Configured cross-origin resource sharing
- **Role-based Access** - OWNER, ADMIN, MEMBER roles

## 📦 Production Deployment

### Prerequisites for Production

Create a `.env` file with production values:
```env
########################################
# == Ports / Published/Internal ==
########################################
TRAEFIK_HTTP_PORT=3069
TRAEFIK_DASHBOARD_PORT=8082

APP_INTERNAL_PORT=3000
SERVER_INTERNAL_PORT=5001

MYSQL_PORT=3308
REDIS_PORT=6382

MINIO_API_PORT=9000
MINIO_CONSOLE_PORT=9003


########################################
# == Disaster Recovery (DR MinIO) ==
########################################
DR_ENDPOINT=http://your-backup-server:9000
DR_MINIO_ROOT_USER=minioadmin
DR_MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=your-secure-dr-password
DR_BUCKET_NAME=inventory-app-backup

MC_INSECURE=0


########################################
# == MySQL ==
########################################
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=<strong-random-password>
MYSQL_DATABASE=inventory_software_prod
MYSQL_USER=appuser
MYSQL_PASSWORD=<strong-random-password>
MYSQL_ROOT_HOST=%
MYSQL_HOST=localhost

# Note: In production containers, these will be overridden to use mysql:3306
DATABASE_URL=mysql://${MYSQL_USER}:${MYSQL_PASSWORD}@${MYSQL_HOST}:${MYSQL_PORT}/${MYSQL_DATABASE}
DATABASE_URL_ROOT=mysql://root:${MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD}@${MYSQL_HOST}:${MYSQL_PORT}/${MYSQL_DATABASE}
SHADOW_DATABASE_URL=mysql://root:${MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD}@${MYSQL_HOST}:${MYSQL_PORT}/inventory_software_prod_shadow


########################################
# == Redis ==
########################################
REDIS_HOST=127.0.0.1


########################################
# == MinIO (Local) ==
########################################
MINIO_ROOT_USER=minioadmin
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=<strong-random-password>
BUCKET_NAME=inventory-app
BUCKET_REGION=us-east-1
MINIO_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:${MINIO_API_PORT}


########################################
# == App Misc ==
########################################
DEV_MODE=false
NODE_ENV=production
SESSION_SECRET=<strong-random-secret-min-64-chars>
USER_ID_ADMIN_MYSQL=<your-admin-user-id>
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION=1.0.0

# Update to your production domain
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://yourdomain.com/api
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://yourdomain.com
BACKEND_ORIGIN=https://yourdomain.com


########################################
# == Email ==
########################################
DONOTREPLY_EMAIL=noreply@yourdomain.com
GOOGLE_EMAIL_USER=noreply@yourdomain.com
GOOGLE_APP_PASSWORD=<your-google-app-password>
```

### Build and Deploy
```bash
# Build Docker images and start all services
pnpm prod:build

# View logs
docker compose -p nova-prod logs -f

# Stop all services
docker compose -p nova-prod down

# Restart a specific service
docker compose -p nova-prod restart server
```

### Database Migrations

Migrations run automatically via the `prisma-migrate` service when containers start. To manually run migrations:
```bash
docker compose -p nova-prod run --rm prisma-migrate npx prisma migrate deploy
```

### Backups

MySQL backups run automatically via cron (default: 3 AM UTC daily). To trigger a manual backup:
```bash
docker compose -p nova-prod exec mysql-dump-to-minio sh -c "export RUN_ONCE=1 && /path/to/backup/script"
```

Backups are stored in MinIO at: `${BACKUP_BUCKET_NAME}/mysql/YYYYMMDDHHMM.${MYSQL_DATABASE}.sql.gz`

